   "ts_ms": 1783386912028,
   "ts_iso": "2026-07-07T01:15:12.028000+00:00",
   "from_me": true,
   "sender_jid": null,
   "type": 0,
   "text": "Or to compare with what you got on the outing with Sonia",
   "starred": false
  },
  {
   "id": 1824830,
   "key_id": "AC690477F70446E34561BA02C03489EC",
   "ts_ms": 1783388099000,
   "ts_iso": "2026-07-07T01:34:59+00:00",
   "from_me": false,
   "sender_jid": null,
   "type": 0,
   "text": "Today I was thinking about how I could build a beautiful arched bridge myself using concrete, rocks, and natural stone in a classic Italian style. The bridge should be strong enough to safely support heavy machinery, ideally with a load capacity of around 6 to 8 tons.\nI was also thinking about how I could build three small dams using the existing concrete structure. The dams should be easy and quick to open and close.\nWhat can we do about termite mounds? Is there a way to prevent them, or is it simply something we have to live with?\nIf a tree is already infested with termites, is there anything that can still be done to save it?\nCan important trees be protected from termites and leafcutter ants? If so, what are the best natural or environmentally friendly methods?\nWhat can we do about leafcutter ants in the most biological and natural way possible?\nWhat kinds of natural stone are available in Paraguay and the surrounding countries that are reasonably affordable? For example, something similar to the flagstone suppliers we have in the Netherlands.\nAre there any good local suppliers of natural stone that you would recommend?",
   "starred": false
  },
  {
   "id": 1824831,
   "key_id": "AC2C124739A75148FEA7C621A76CC7AA",
   "ts_ms": 1783388172000,
   "ts_iso": "2026-07-07T01:36:12+00:00",
   "from_me": false,
   "sender_jid": null,
   "type": 0,
